; Where each frame is in its sentence's fall to the end. Per segment two cards in (n, send); at a sentence's first
; frame its summary (L, to, M, end; INP at gl); per frame two cards out: y, how far into the fall in hundredths (-1
; before frame to, or with no fall), and the end (1 a statement, 2 a question). y = 100 (f - to) / M by Bresenham:
; each frame past to adds 100 to yr and takes M away as often as it goes; at most 100.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            seg     INP   i        03-11: a segment (i counts its frames down)
  04                    INP   send
  05            frm     CLA   i
  06                    SUB   00
  07                    TAC   eos
  08                    STO   i
  09                    CLA   ns
  10                    SUB   00
  11                    TAC   go
  12            gl      INP   x        12-20: a new sentence's summary
  13            g2      INP   to
  14            g3      INP   m
  15            g4      INP   end
  16                    CLA   z
  17                    STO   f
  18                    STO   y
  19                    STO   yr
  20                    STO   ns
  21            go      CLA   to       21-32: y (or -1) and the end out
  22                    TAC   none
  23                    CLA   f
  24                    SUB   to
  25                    TAC   none
  26                    OUT   y
  27                    JMP   nx
  28            none    OUT   m1
  29            nx      OUT   end
  30                    CLA   f
  31                    ADD   00
  32                    STO   f
  33                    CLA   to       33-59: y on a frame, past to
  34                    TAC   frm
  35                    CLA   to
  36                    SUB   f
  37                    TAC   yu
  38                    JMP   frm
  39            yu      CLA   y
  40                    SUB   c100
  41                    TAC   yg
  42                    JMP   frm
  43            yg      CLA   yr
  44                    ADD   c100
  45                    STO   yr
  46            yl      CLA   yr
  47                    SUB   m
  48                    TAC   yc
  49                    STO   yr
  50                    CLA   y
  51                    ADD   00
  52                    STO   y
  53                    JMP   yl
  54            yc      CLA   y
  55                    SUB   c100
  56                    TAC   frm
  57                    CLA   c100
  58                    STO   y
  59                    JMP   frm
  60            eos     CLA   send     60-65: the segment ends a sentence: the next frame starts one
  61                    SUB   00
  62                    TAC   seg
  63                    CLA   00
  64                    STO   ns
  65                    JMP   seg
  70            i       DATA  0
  71            send    DATA  0
  72            ns      DATA  1
  73            x       DATA  0
  74            to      DATA  0
  75            m       DATA  0
  76            end     DATA  0
  77            f       DATA  0
  78            y       DATA  0
  79            yr      DATA  0
  80            z       DATA  0
  81            m1      DATA  -1
  82            c100    DATA  100
